# Repository Guidelines

## Project Overview

Describe the project's purpose and list each module or major package with one responsibility.

## Technology Baseline

- Java: record the exact version from the build.
- Build: record Maven or Gradle and the wrapper/version policy.
- Frameworks: record the exact Spring, RPC, persistence, and test stack already in use.

## Project Structure

List production source, resources, migrations, generated code, and test directories. State where controllers, services, DAOs, entities, request objects, and configuration live.

## Build, Test, and Run Commands

- Full build: provide the exact command.
- Focused test: provide the exact module and single-test command.
- Local run: provide the exact command and name external prerequisites without including secrets.

## Local Conventions

Record only conventions unique to this repository: module boundaries, package names, approved libraries, generated-file rules, and compatibility exceptions. Do not duplicate the global Dayima Java conventions.

## Security and Configuration

Identify sensitive configuration locations and approved local override mechanisms. Never include credentials, tokens, private keys, production endpoints, or real user data.
